## Accordion — Contained

::: accordion {style=outline}
:: Lockout/Tagout
Confirm equipment is de-energized before maintenance.

:: PPE Check
Verify gloves, eyewear, and hearing protection before work starts.

:: Incident Report
Document all near-miss events within 24 hours.
:::

## Accordion — Separated

::: accordion {style=shaded}
:: Module 1
Introduction to workplace safety regulations.

:: Module 2
Advanced hazard identification techniques.
:::

## Tabs

::: tabs {orientation=vertical style=pills}
:: Incident Types
Near miss, first aid, recordable, and lost-time incidents.

:: Response Flow
Stop work, secure area, notify supervisor, and document details.

:: Follow-Up
Review, re-train, and update procedures as needed.
:::

## Columns

Three-column comparison of risk management approaches.

::: columns
::
**Hazards** — Chemical, biological, physical, and ergonomic risks.

::
**Controls** — Engineering, administrative, and PPE-based solutions.

::
**Review** — Annual audits and monthly spot checks.
:::

## Sequence — Numbered

::: sequence {style=numbered}
:: 1. Identify Hazard
Report any unsafe condition immediately.

:: 2. Assess Risk
Determine severity and likelihood of harm.

:: 3. Apply Controls
Implement engineering or procedural safeguards.

:: 4. Monitor
Verify controls remain effective over time.
:::

## Sequence — Timeline

::: sequence {style=timeline}
:: 2020 — Foundation
Established initial safety protocols.

:: 2022 — Expansion
Added chemical handling procedures.

:: 2024 — Automation
Deployed IoT monitoring sensors.
:::

## Sequence — Plain

::: sequence {style=none}
:: Observation
Note conditions before starting work.

:: Action
Apply controls and begin task.

:: Verification
Confirm controls held throughout.
:::

## Comparison

::: comparison {layout=side-by-side}
:: Before
Manual incident logging with paper forms, 48-hour reporting delay.

:: After
Digital incident capture with real-time alerts, under 2-hour response.
:::

## Single Choice

::: choice Which action should happen first after spotting a hazard? {scored}
( ) Continue working while monitoring
(x) Stop work and secure the area
( ) Wait until shift handoff
:::

## Single Choice — Shuffled with Feedback

::: choice What is the minimum PPE for construction zones? {scored shuffle}
( ) Hard hat only
(x) Hard hat, safety glasses, and high-vis vest
feedback: Correct! All three are required.
( ) Steel-toed boots only
feedback: Important but insufficient on its own.
:::

