# Cards
::: cards Safety Terms {layout=slides transition=fade showProgress}
:: What is PPE? {level=3}
Personal Protective Equipment refers to protective clothing, helmets, goggles, or other garments designed to protect the wearer's body from injury or infection.
::: back
Use PPE when residual hazard remains after engineering and administrative controls.
:::
:: When is PPE required? {level=3}
Whenever there is a risk of injury from hazards that cannot be eliminated through engineering or administrative controls.
::: back
PPE is the final layer in the hierarchy of controls, not the first control.
:::
:::
::: cards
:: What does LOTO stand for?
::: back
Lockout / Tagout — the process of isolating energy sources before maintenance.
:::
:::
